        {
          "type": "note",
          "tone": "warning",
          "title": "Gotchas",
          "text": "- Il y a + a length of time = ago: Il y a six mois, Hugo a demandé Camille en mariage. It is the same il y a as « there is », but the meaning comes from the time word after it.\n- Samedi dernier (no article) = last Saturday, once. Le samedi = every Saturday (a habit). The same difference as in Leçon 16.\n- Demander quelqu'un en mariage = to propose to someone (literally “ask someone in marriage”). The couple get married: se marier (pronominal verb). Épouser quelqu'un also means to marry someone: Il épouse Camille.\n- Un fiancé / une fiancée = fiancé(e). Le fiancé de Camille. Un spectateur is a member of an audience; un spectacle is a show.\n- In France the civil marriage takes place at the town hall (la mairie), the PACS (pacte civil de solidarité) is another legal form of union."
        },
        {
